WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.028
There are two kinds of weather in Thailand: wet and dry.

2
00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:08.053
From April to October it rains every day.

3
00:00:08.054 --> 00:00:13.118
Almost six hundred years ago, there was a terrible storm in a city called Chiang Mai.

4
00:00:13.119 --> 00:00:22.991
It happened in 1434. Even though there was a strong wind, loud thunder, and deep puddles of rain, the people of Chiang Mai were not afraid.

5
00:00:22.992 --> 00:00:26.935
They were used to storms.

6
00:00:26.936 --> 00:00:29.552
Outside the city was a small temple.

7
00:00:29.553 --> 00:00:34.525
There was a monk who lived at this temple and took care of the statues of Buddha.

8
00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:39.834
Whenever storms came, the monk would protect the incense so it didn't get wet.

9
00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:43.594
He wanted the incense to burn for Buddha.

10
00:00:43.595 --> 00:00:48.600
After cleaning the temple, the monk stood in the doorway to watch the storm.

11
00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:52.039
The lightning stretched its fingers across the sky.

12
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.926
The storm was coming closer to the temple. Just

13
00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:59.643
then, the monk saw a flash and heard a large crack! The

14
00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:03.647
lightning struck a chedi outside the temple and broke it. A

15
00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:06.360
chedi is a bell-shaped pagoda. The

16
00:01:06.361 --> 00:01:12.406
first chedis contained the ashes of the Buddha and all chedis are sacred to his memory. The

17
00:01:12.407 --> 00:01:15.185
monk ran out into the rain. He

18
00:01:15.186 --> 00:01:20.505
wanted to protect the memory of Buddha preserved in the broken chedi .

19
00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:26.367
The monk found an object on the ground, among the stone pieces from the broken chedi

20
00:01:26.368 --> 00:01:30.610
. He wrapped the object in his robes and carried it into the

21
00:01:30.611 --> 00:01:33.588
temple. He lit a candle to see what it

22
00:01:33.589 --> 00:01:38.711
was. It looked like a statue of Buddha made out of

23
00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:45.801
rock. Because the statue was small, and it did not look valuable, the monk put the statue in his

24
00:01:45.802 --> 00:01:52.175
house. Every day he would clean this statue of Buddha and pray to

25
00:01:52.176 --> 00:01:55.361
it. The monk took care of the statue for many

26
00:01:55.362 --> 00:01:59.526
years. But one day, when he was cleaning the statue, the nose fell

27
00:01:59.527 --> 00:02:03.886
off. "Oh no!" the monk cried. Then he looked

28
00:02:03.887 --> 00:02:07.847
again. There was another nose underneath, and it was

29
00:02:07.848 --> 00:02:10.901
green! The monk carefully began to pull away the

30
00:02:10.902 --> 00:02:14.364
rock. Underneath was a second Buddha made of

31
00:02:14.365 --> 00:02:20.955
jade. The green was such a beautiful green that he named the statue The Emerald

32
00:02:20.956 --> 00:02:25.696
Buddha. The monk sent a letter to the king, telling him the story of the Emerald

33
00:02:25.697 --> 00:02:28.403
Buddha. King Samfangkaen was

34
00:02:28.404 --> 00:02:32.330
excited. He asked for the statue to be sent to his palace in Chiang

35
00:02:32.331 --> 00:02:35.630
Mai. The monk was sad to see the Emerald Buddha

36
00:02:35.631 --> 00:02:39.464
go. He put it on an elephant and sent it to Chiang Mai.

37
00:02:39.465 --> 00:02:44.056
But when the elephant got to the road, it would not go to Chiang Mai.

38
00:02:44.057 --> 00:02:48.430
This made the king angry, so he sent another elephant.

39
00:02:48.431 --> 00:02:51.882
This elephant would not go to Chiang Mai either.

40
00:02:51.883 --> 00:02:56.196
The king was very angry, so he sent a third elephant.

41
00:02:56.197 --> 00:03:01.173
This elephant did exactly what the first two had done.

42
00:03:01.174 --> 00:03:07.717
The king thought, "Maybe the Emerald Buddha doesn't want to leave," so he stopped sending elephants.

43
00:03:07.718 --> 00:03:14.598
The jade statue of Buddha stayed with the monk for 32 more years.

44
00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:20.396
Today the Emerald Buddha is kept in a temple called Wat Phra Kaew in Bangkok, Thailand.

45
00:03:20.397 --> 00:03:26.300
Three times a year there is a special ceremony when the king changes the clothes of the Emerald Buddha.

46
00:03:26.301 --> 00:03:29.076
The Emerald Buddha was a hidden treasure.

47
00:03:29.077 --> 00:03:33.810
What other hidden treasures are there waiting to be discovered?

